The Tru64 V5.1B system is actually just two disks that slide easily in
the AS800. I figured that installing, deleting and reinstalling the
various DECnet components had messed up the OS installation as well.
So I reinstalled Tru64 and the procedure reported a disk failure, it
couldn't restart the os.
With one new disk I tried V5.0 and this os version installed properly
and I found a DECnet options set that worked.
Right now I'm in the process of a V5.1B reinstall. But it seems my
problem was hardware not software.

Thanks all of you who helped me find the DECnet product and sort out
its installation details.
Hans


