I've tried to install DECnet OSI 5.0 on three different Tru64
versions: V5.0, V5.1A and V5.1B.
The DECnet kit is called dna500 and I have this kit on two different
cd sets (October 1999 and January 2000).
Both sets show the same behaviour: they both work on Tru64 V5.0 and
fail to work on 5.1A and 5.1B.
The installation performs flawlessly, running decnetsetup basic (and
advanced for that matter) gives an error message that certain kernel
component(s) weren't loaded properly. No further details on what
components or why they failed to load.
I assume that there is a version mismatch between the os kernel and
the DNA kits. The three os installations were full installations, all
options were selected during the os installation procedure.
Which prompts the question whether a kind soul would send me the
DECnet OSI kit for Tru64 V5.1 A (and possibly also for 5.1 B).

Side note:
I run Tru64 V5.0 at home for hobbyist reasons. One system came with
the required licenses so that's legal. I ran the other versions on
another machine (and copied the PAK's) just to figure out whether I
had all the components to upgrade to V5.1A.
Hans


