Michael,
admittedly, the nomenclature for the product is confusing for me.
DECnet OSI on Tru64 does what DECnet Plus is for VMS.
Which is a DECnet phase 5 implementation. I run DECnet phase 5 on a
few VAX/VMS systems because at that time I worked for a company that
had migrated entirely to phase 5. It is a well tought out well
designed and good implemented product. IIRC Yannick Pouffary presented
many DECnet phase 5 presentations at DECUS to convince us all to
upgrade our existing phase IV implementations.
The thing is of course that once you've mastered the less than 10 most
useful NCP commands, the thought of having to learn many more and far
more complicated ncl commands was somewhat daunting :)
I'd rather run phase IV on my Tru64 system but AFAIK that product
doesn't exist for V5.x
A long winded begin of an answer but my question is whether you would
be so kind to let me have a copy of that Compaq DECnet-Plus kit?
Hans



