> > Hans
>
> There are two different versions of DECnet-plus on the SPL disks one for
> DU V4.x and one for Tru64 V5.x.
> In your case the version for V5.x is of course the right one.
> It resides on disk 2.
>
> The Installation guide is there:http://h30266.www3.hp.com/masterindex/ins=
tallation_guide/installation...
>
> Shortcut:
>
> # setld -l <path-to-kit> <kitname>
>
> Kari

On a Tru64 V5.0 system the decnet kit is called DNABASE500. I'd
expected to find something like DNABASE510 on one of the four Tru64
cd's in the Operating system kit. I found nothing. Luckily the V5.1
cd's are readable on a Windows XP system because the AS300 cdrom drive
went south, I hope it's just a matter of temperature.
The four disks in the V5.1A operating system kit are labeled:
Operating System, volume 1,
Associated Products, volume 1,
Associated Products, volume 2,
Documentation
The cluster manual for V5.1A mentions DECnet as a possible transport,
that's all I could find.
Hans

BTW in Tru64 V5 the device names changed, a cdrom is called /dev/disk/
cdrom0c


